{"id":31268277574,"name":"Run api tests","node_id":"WFR_kwLOA_1uaM8AAAAHR7wNRg","head_branch":"fix/2.41-optionset-preheat-n1","head_sha":"85632e1858b43c4277aefbea0592e29ee10c8c98","path":".github/workflows/run-api-tests.yml","run_number":51880,"run_attempt":1,"event":"pull_request","display_title":"perf: stop preheat from fully materializing OptionSet.options","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","workflow_id":5591308,"check_suite_id":84839206867,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDOA_1uaM8AAAATwM-P0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31268277574","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31268277574","pull_requests":[{"id":4235305546,"number":24813,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/pulls/24813","head":{"ref":"fix/2.41-optionset-preheat-n1","sha":"6781db3dea0ec32f7dedf39478f2aacef39cbe87","repo":{"id":66940520,"name":"dhis2-core","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core"}},"base":{"ref":"2.41","sha":"1ac3fe5bd911fb3fb3c36885154fa5e7df37d97a","repo":{"id":66940520,"name":"dhis2-core","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core"}}}],"created_at":"2026-08-08T16:58:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-08T17:13:18Z","run_started_at":"2026-08-08T16:58:45Z","jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31268277574/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31268277574/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/check-suites/84839206867","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31268277574/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31268277574/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31268277574/rerun","head_commit":{"message":"fix: resolve option codes introduced by program rule ASSIGN actions\n\nThe tracker import preheat only resolves the (option set, code) pairs the\nimport payload actually references, so validation can check option codes\nwithout materializing whole OptionSet.options collections. Program rule\nASSIGN actions break that assumption: they can add or overwrite data values\nand attributes that were not in the payload, so the codes they introduce\nwere never resolved and valid data was rejected with E1125.\n\nFix it where the assigned values first become known: the values an ASSIGN\naction will apply are the rule engine's already evaluated output, captured\nin the Assign*Executor objects that calculateRuleEffects builds from\nRuleEffects#getData. Nothing evaluated later can change them, so right\nafter calculateRuleEffects returns we can collect every (target, value)\npair from those executors and resolve it through OptionValueSupplier's\nexisting entry point, all within the same \"Running Rule Engine\" stage. No\nvalidator chain changes are needed, and the whole bundle costs one batched\nquery, or none at all when no ASSIGN action is present.\n\nNote the injection point matters. Doing this over the bundle's entities\ninstead of its executors would be a no-op: calculateRuleEffects only\ncomputes RuleEffects, it mutates nothing. The mutations happen later, per\nentity, inside the rule engine validators, interleaved with the very\nvalidators that read the resolved codes, so there is no whole-bundle\nboundary in between where the mutated entities could be re-read.\n\nIdentifiers are converted with TrackerPreheat#getIdSchemes, the same way\nthe executors convert them when applying a value, because preheat metadata\nis keyed by the payload's id scheme, not by UID.\n\nAlso adds a diagnostic warning distinguishing \"this code was checked and\ndoes not exist\" from \"this option set was never resolved\", the latter being\nan internal bug rather than user error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","author":{"name":"Jason Pickering","email":"jason@dhis2.org"},"id":"85632e1858b43c4277aefbea0592e29ee10c8c98","tree_id":"336c5203028e89c0c785173c38e8257097320aa8","timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:14:25Z","committer":{"name":"Jason Pickering","email":"jason@dhis2.org"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/5591308","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2Njk0MDUyMA==","owner":{"login":"dhis2","id":1089987,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEwODk5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1089987?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2","gravatar_id":"","type":"Organization","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/subscriptions"},"name":"dhis2-core","full_name":"dhis2/dhis2-core","description":"DHIS 2 Core. Written in Java. Contains the service layer and Web API.","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core","fork":false,"private":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/{archive_format}{/ref}","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/assignees{/user}","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/git/blobs{/sha}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/branches{/branch}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/collaborators{/collaborator}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/comments{/number}","commits_url":"https://api.